  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A wire of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>$R_{1}$ is drawn out so that its length is increased by twice of its original length. The ratio of new resistance to original resistance is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zvy99",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "BOd6k",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>9</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KdYk7",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5u69M",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>As per the given question, the change in the length is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>l</mi></math>.</p><p>Resistance of a wire is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>When the length is starched by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, final length will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. As the volume remains constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>&#961;</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
